{"episodes":{"187579":"Morning and afternoon severe thunderstorms developed ahead of a cold front and produced wind damage and hail. Several spotters also reported funnel clouds.","187583":"A slow-moving storm system brought several inches of rainfall to most of Central Alabama from early morning on February 11 through the evening of February 12. While most areas saw at least 1-2 inches of rain, parts of southern and southeastern Central Alabama recorded as much as 8 inches, especially across parts of Lee, Macon, and Russell counties. Waves of heavy rainfall resulted in flooding along the Interstate 85 corridor during the afternoon of February 11 and again during the early morning of February 12. More storms formed in western and central parts of the area around midday February 12, ahead of an approaching cold front. A few of these storms produced hail up to penny to quarter size, notably around Tuscaloosa and Hoover, along with sporadic tree damage. After the frontal passage, flooding of large streams and creeks in Russell and Macon counties continued into February 13.","188912":"Thunderstorms developed along a stationary front over South Central Texas. Some of these storms produced large hail.","188967":"A broken line of thunderstorms moved through Central Texas the night of February 10th into the 11th. The line and clusters of storms south of the line produced large hail generally in a line from Comanche to Hillsboro to Athens/Palestine.","188988":"A warm front lifted north across Southeast Texas ahead of an approaching low pressure system. Scattered showers and storms occurred along the boundary with a couple becoming severe.","188989":"A warm front lifted north across the region early during the 11th ahead of an approaching low pressure system. Scattered thunderstorms develop along the warm front with some becoming severe. Another round of thunderstorm occurred as the low pressure system and associated cold front moved through late on the 11th into the 12th.","189046":"Numerous severe thunderstorms developed in the early morning hours on February 11th along and ahead of a slowly advancing cold front stretching across East Texas and North Louisiana. Strong southwesterly winds in the mid-levels and associated 45-55 knots of deep-layer shear combined to support sustained updrafts, including within a few supercell thunderstorms. Steep lapse rates aloft and a rich, moist low-level air mass present along and south of the boundary indicated moderate instability, with MLCAPE generally from 1500-2000 J/kg. Large hail, some greater than 2 inches in diameter, was the resulting primary severe threat while isolated severe and damaging wind gusts proved to be a secondary threat in the convective downdrafts. Numerous reports of mostly large to very large hail were received across parts of East Texas and North Louisiana along with a few damaging wind reports.","189048":"Numerous severe thunderstorms developed in the early morning hours on February 11th along and ahead of a slowly advancing cold front stretching across East Texas and North Louisiana. Strong southwesterly winds in the mid-levels and associated 45-55 knots of deep-layer shear combined to support sustained updrafts, including within a few supercell thunderstorms. Steep lapse rates aloft and a rich, moist low-level air mass present along and south of the boundary indicated moderate instability, with MLCAPE generally from 1500-2000 J/kg. Large hail, some greater than 2 inches in diameter, was the resulting primary severe threat while isolated severe and damaging wind gusts proved to be a secondary threat in the convective downdrafts. Numerous reports of mostly large to very large hail were received across parts of East Texas and North Louisiana along with a few damaging wind reports.","189154":"Scattered thunderstorms developed across much of west central Texas during the late evening of February 10th and the early morning hours of February 11th. Several of the storms were severe and produced large hail.","189348":"Heavy rain from thunderstorms resulted in flooding due to rises in creeks across portions of Walker County.","189442":"Severe thunderstorms occurred across portions of Mississippi along a stalled frontal boundary that had settled into the area.","189443":"Severe thunderstorms occurred across portions of Louisiana along a stalled frontal boundary that had settled into the area."},"events":[{"begin":"2024-02-11T01:00Z","county":"Walker","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-02-11T03:00Z","endLat":30.6314,"endLon":-95.6111,"episode":189348,"id":1164476,"injuries":0,"lat":30.6321,"location":"4.11 NNW East Sandy","lon":-95.6134,"narrative":"Heavy rain from thunderstorms resulted in flooding along Bowden Rd at Robinson Creek.","source":"Emergency Manager","state":"TX","type":"Flood","wfo":"HGX"},{"begin":"2024-02-11T01:30Z","county":"Walker","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-02-11T03:30Z","endLat":30.8668,"endLon":-95.7168,"episode":189348,"id":1164477,"injuries":0,"lat":30.87,"location":"3.27 ENE Mossy Grove","lon":-95.72,"narrative":"Heavy rain from thunderstorms resulted in flooding along FM2989 at Bedias Creek.","source":"Emergency Manager","state":"TX","type":"Flood","wfo":"HGX"},{"begin":"2024-02-11T05:03Z","county":"Taylor","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-02-11T05:03Z","endLat":32.18,"endLon":-99.77,"episode":189154,"id":1163209,"injuries":0,"lat":32.18,"location":"3.27 SSE Tuscola","lon":-99.77,"magnitude":1.0,"narrative":"Public reported quarter size hail.","source":"Public","state":"TX","type":"Hail","wfo":"SJT"},{"begin":"2024-02-11T05:14Z","county":"Scott","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"2.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-02-11T05:14Z","endLat":32.354,"endLon":-89.689,"episode":189442,"id":1165041,"injuries":0,"lat":32.354,"location":"1.14 WNW Morton","lon":-89.689,"magnitude":48.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative"